{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8683b5a-1bb3-40f7-aff9-33655508a2e2","agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no searching. Memory limited: one 400px CDP screenshot of the bench (cleanup via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py). Report under 100 words. Files: NEW cuore/services/bench_bridge.py, cuore/web/bench_routes.py, cuore/web/templates/bench.html, cuore/tests/check_bench.py; edits: cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py (verdict next_action only), cuore/web/routes.py (make GET /v/{vin} render the bench and move the old dossier to GET /v/{vin}/dossier), cuore/app.py (register bench_routes if you put the route there instead). Do not edit base.html, _vbar.html, _flow_bar.html, _vtabs.html, job.html, vehicle.html, systems.*, codes templates, cuore.css (other agents).\n\nRepo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; tests use a temp CUORE_STATE_DIR. Data: dossier_bridge.build_view (verdict, open_work steps with done flags, codes, freeze_frames with fuel flags, bulletins), parts_bridge.parts_for_code, tools_kb_bridge (recommend per step), shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name / current visit (complaint), flow_bridge.flow_state, cases_bridge.prefill, i18n `t()` global, `icon()` global, `static_url` global.\n\n1. dossier_bridge: add `verdict.next_action` (one sentence, computed, sourced): combine the blockers: if any EVAP freeze frame fuel > 85 % or < 15 % and verdict is UNVERIFIED_REPAIR: \"Cannot verify yet: the EVAP monitor will not run above 85 % fuel (set at {pct} %). Burn fuel into the 15-85 % window, then complete a drive cycle. Meanwhile: {first unchecked open-work step} ({its bulletin}).\"; if ACTIVE_FAULTS: \"Start with {first unchecked step} ({bulletin}).\"; if VERIFIED_CLEAN: \"Verified by readiness read on {date}: release.\"; NO_DATA: \"Read the car.\" Also `verdict.blocker` (short label) and `verdict.next_step_id`.\n2. bench_bridge.build_bench(vin) -> {vehicle (decoded name, never \"(unnamed vehicle)\"), vin_tail, km, complaint (current visit or None), verdict (state, label, sentence, next_action, blocker), next_actions: top 3 unchecked open-work steps across families ordered ACTIVE first then by family priority, each {step_id, family, text, bulletin ref, parts: [{name, number, confidence}] (parts_for_code of the family's codes, max 3), tools: [{name, have}] (tools_kb recommend for the step key when one exists, max 4), done: False, href_tick: the existing POST /v/{vin}/checklist form}, open_codes_count, last_read: date, shortcuts: [code page links for active/cleared codes (max 6)], case_hint: one line from cases_bridge.prefill if any}.\n3. bench.html: no hero, no step bar; fits one 400x800 screen without scrolling for the top: a 40px status line (vehicle name, VIN tail, km, verdict chip), the complaint in quotes, the next_action sentence large (20px) under the verdict chip, then the 3 next actions as big cards: checkbox form (44px) + text + bulletin chip + parts line + tools line with have/not; then one row of shortcut chips (codes), and links \"Job\", \"Full dossier\". Pictograms via icon(); labels via t() with it/en keys added to cuore/web/i18n.py.\n4. Routes: GET /v/{vin} -> bench (keep `tab=\"bench\"`), GET /v/{vin}/dossier -> old dossier page (same handler, tab \"dossier\"). Checks (5): bench 200 for the Stelvio with \"Stelvio\" in the status line and no \"(unnamed vehicle)\"; verdict next_action mentions 85 % and a bulletin for this VIN; 3 next actions with at least one part number; /v/{vin}/dossier still 200 (check_dossier_page.py may need its URL changed to /dossier: do it); 400px screenshot: the first next-action card's top is within the viewport height (bounding box top < 800) with no horizontal overflow. Run check_bench.py, check_dossier_page.py, check_dossier_view.py, check_api.py."},"uuid":"da538fb0-c248-473e-a3ed-9791c34d5673","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:02:44.004Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
