{"parentUuid":"a4dd4d5d-1b47-49ad-bda8-d135496d0b42","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpyQmn1GFPsd4cJjs53b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RqVMsgMmZjwRFhUDVy7Kue","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\parts_bridge.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16504,"cache_read_input_tokens":82918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16504,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RqVMsgMmZjwRFhUDVy7Kue":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\parts_bridge.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f78b0ee6-3100-4f3c-be9c-92c14033f6bb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfpyQmUQWxgKYX93bWBni","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ce40408-c5fb-450e-83db-7995f230482a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:09.012Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"3ce40408-c5fb-450e-83db-7995f230482a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8683b5a-1bb3-40f7-aff9-33655508a2e2","agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RqVMsgMmZjwRFhUDVy7Kue","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"The only module in CUORE that imports :mod:`mes.parts`.\n2\t\n3\t``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` is being written in parallel by another agent\n4\tand may not exist yet. Every call into it is wrapped and falls back to a\n5\tbuilt-in fixture (shaped exactly like that module's documented contract --\n6\tsee ``_FIXTURE`` below) so the parts page, the ``/api/parts*`` endpoints and\n7\tthe part cards embedded in ``code.html``/``maintenance.html``/\n8\t``oil_change.html``/``brakes_tires.html`` are developable and testable\n9\tbefore it lands. Once ``mes.parts`` exists, nothing here needs to change --\n10\tthe lazy import just starts succeeding and the fixture stops being reached.\n11\t\n12\tContract (``mes.parts``, once it lands): ``get(key)``, ``for_code(code)``,\n13\t``for_job(job)``, ``all()``, each returning / each row shaped::\n14\t\n15\t    {key, name, what_it_does,\n16\t     oem: [{number, brand, note, confidence, source}],\n17\t     supersedes, aftermarket: [{brand, number, confidence, source}],\n18\t     fits, location, related_codes, related_jobs, torque_keys,\n19\t     price: {low, high, currency, as_of, source} | None,\n20\t     buy: [{label, url}],\n21\t     images: [{url, source_page, source_name, kind, licence_note, verified_at}],\n22\t     notes}\n23\t\n24\t``torque_keys`` is a list of keys into the torque libraries -- resolved\n25\there, not by ``mes.parts`` itself, against ``mes.service_specs`` and\n26\t``mes.drivetrain_specs`` (the same two libraries\n27\t``cuore.services.service_bridge`` already reaches through its own bridge),\n28\tso a part card can show \"25 Nm, SINGLE-SOURCE\" without ``mes.parts`` needing\n29\tto duplicate the torque library. A key neither library recognises resolves\n30\tto an UNKNOWN row rather than being dropped, so the card can say so.\n31\t\n32\tEvery public function here degrades to an empty result (\"No part data yet\")\n33\trather than raising -- the one exception is :func:`part`, which returns\n34\t``None`` for an unknown key so the API layer can turn that into a 404.\n35\t\"\"\"\n36\t\n37\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n38\t\n39\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n40\t\n41\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n42\t\n43\t\n44\t# --- lazy imports, each independently guarded ------------------------------\n45\t\n46\tdef _parts_mod():\n47\t    \"\"\"``mes.parts``, or ``None`` if it has not landed yet.\"\"\"\n48\t    try:\n49\t        from mes import parts as parts_mod\n50\t        return parts_mod\n51\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- must never be why a page 500s\n52\t        return None\n53\t\n54\t\n55\tdef _service_specs():\n56\t    try:\n57\t        from mes import service_specs\n58\t        return service_specs\n59\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n60\t        return None\n61\t\n62\t\n63\tdef _drivetrain_specs():\n64\t    try:\n65\t        from mes import drivetrain_specs\n66\t        return drivetrain_specs\n67\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n68\t        return None\n69\t\n70\t\n71\tdef _model_for_vin(vin: Optional[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n72\t    \"\"\"Best-effort model name for ``vin`` via ``mes.platform``, or ``None``\n73\t    on any failure or an unrecognised VIN -- never raises.\"\"\"\n74\t    if not vin:\n75\t        return None\n76\t    try:\n77\t        from mes import platform as platform_mod\n78\t        model = platform_mod.model_for_vin(vin)\n79\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n80\t        return None\n81\t    return None if model == \"UNKNOWN\" else model\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t# --- fixture: the exact shape mes.parts.get()/for_code()/for_job()/all()\n85\t# will return, used until that module lands (or for any key it does not yet\n86\t# cover). Keyed to things this corpus already knows about -- the Stelvio's\n87\t# chronic P0455/P0456 EVAP family (see project_stelvio_evap.md) and the jobs\n88\t# oil_change.html/maintenance.html/brakes_tires.html already render -- so a\n89\t# developer working on those pages sees real-looking cards immediately. ----\n90\t\n91\t_FIXTURE: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {\n92\t    \"esim\": {\n93\t        \"key\": \"esim\",\n94\t        \"name\": \"EVAP Service/Integrity Monitor (ESIM)\",\n95\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Pressurizes the fuel-vapor system and watches the \"\n96\t                        \"decay rate to detect small and large EVAP leaks. A \"\n97\t                        \"failed self-test or a failed component sets \"\n98\t                        \"P0455/P0456/P0457, not necessarily a leak itself.\",\n99\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68245527AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n100\t                 \"note\": \"ESIM / natural-vacuum leak-detection pump assembly\",\n101\t                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n102\t                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\"}],\n103\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n104\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Standard Motor Products\", \"number\": \"EVAP1234\",\n105\t                         \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None}],\n106\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n107\t        \"location\": \"Rear of the fuel tank, inline on the vapor line, ahead of the canister.\",\n108\t        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"P0457\"],\n109\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n110\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_esim_mount\"],\n111\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 180.0, \"high\": 260.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n112\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n113\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"},\n114\t                {\"label\": \"Mopar eStore\", \"url\": \"https://www.moparonlineparts.com\"}],\n115\t        \"images\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/data/esim-photo.jpg\",\n116\t                    \"source_page\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\",\n117\t                    \"source_name\": \"stelvioforum.com\", \"kind\": \"product_photo\",\n118\t                    \"licence_note\": \"forum upload, fair-use reference only\",\n119\t                    \"verified_at\": \"2026-09-20\"}],\n120\t        \"notes\": \"Verified against TSB 18-030-17 before replacing -- that TSB's ECM \"\n121\t                 \"calibration read fixes a false P0456 on some build dates without \"\n122\t                 \"any part being replaced.\",\n123\t    },\n124\t    \"purge_valve\": {\n125\t        \"key\": \"purge_valve\",\n126\t        \"name\": \"EVAP Purge Solenoid Valve\",\n127\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Opens under ECM control to let engine vacuum draw stored fuel \"\n128\t                        \"vapor from the canister into the intake. Stuck closed or \"\n129\t                        \"leaking, it can contribute to a P0455/P0456 decay-rate failure.\",\n130\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68093419AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n131\t                 \"note\": \"Purge valve/solenoid\", \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n132\t                 \"source\": \"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/purge-valve-location.9821/\"}],\n133\t        \"supersedes\": [\"68093419A (earlier casting, same fit)\"],\n134\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Four Seasons\", \"number\": \"PV1029\",\n135\t                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n136\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n137\t        \"location\": \"Intake manifold, driver's side, short hose run to the charcoal canister.\",\n138\t        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\"],\n139\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n140\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_purge_valve_mount\"],\n141\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 45.0, \"high\": 90.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n142\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n143\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n144\t        \"images\": [],\n145\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n146\t    },\n147\t    \"oil_filter\": {\n148\t        \"key\": \"oil_filter\",\n149\t        \"name\": \"Engine Oil Filter (cartridge element)\",\n150\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Traps combustion byproducts and wear metal out of circulating oil.\",\n151\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68105175AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"cartridge element + housing cap\",\n152\t                 \"confidence\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n153\t                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/oil-change-maintenance-reset.19336/\"}],\n154\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n155\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Mopar/Mann filter element\", \"number\": \"HU 711/51x\",\n156\t                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n157\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T MultiAir (2017-2022)\",\n158\t        \"location\": \"Top of the engine, cartridge-style housing with a plastic cap.\",\n159\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n160\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"oil_change\"],\n161\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"filter_cap\"],\n162\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 18.0, \"high\": 32.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n163\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n164\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n165\t        \"images\": [],\n166\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n167\t    },\n168\t    \"engine_air_filter\": {\n169\t        \"key\": \"engine_air_filter\",\n170\t        \"name\": \"Engine Air Filter\",\n171\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Keeps intake air clean of dust/debris ahead of the MAF/turbo.\",\n172\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68248729AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"panel element\",\n173\t                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n174\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n175\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"K&N\", \"number\": \"33-5061\", \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n176\t                         \"source\": None}],\n177\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n178\t        \"location\": \"Airbox, passenger side of the engine bay.\",\n179\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n180\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"engine_air_filter\"],\n181\t        \"torque_keys\": [],\n182\t        \"price\": None,\n183\t        \"buy\": [],\n184\t        \"images\": [],\n185\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n186\t    },\n187\t    \"brake_pads_front\": {\n188\t        \"key\": \"brake_pads_front\",\n189\t        \"name\": \"Front Brake Pad Set\",\n190\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Friction material clamped onto the front rotors by the caliper.\",\n191\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68273809AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"front pad set\",\n192\t                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n193\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n194\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Brembo\", \"number\": \"P23165\", \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\",\n195\t                         \"source\": None}],\n196\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio, base brakes (2017-2022)\",\n197\t        \"location\": \"Front calipers.\",\n198\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n199\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"brakes_front\"],\n200\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"caliper_slider_front\"],\n201\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 90.0, \"high\": 160.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n202\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n203\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n204\t        \"images\": [],\n205\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"wheel_lug_bolts\": {\n208\t        \"key\": \"wheel_lug_bolts\",\n209\t        \"name\": \"Wheel Lug Bolts\",\n210\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Clamps the wheel to the hub.\",\n211\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68247068AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"lug bolt, M14\",\n212\t                 \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n213\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n214\t        \"aftermarket\": [],\n215\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio (2017-2022)\",\n216\t        \"location\": \"Each wheel, five per corner.\",\n217\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n218\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"wheels\"],\n219\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"wheel_lug\"],\n220\t        \"price\": None,\n221\t        \"buy\": [],\n222\t        \"images\": [],\n223\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n224\t    },\n225\t}\n226\t\n227\t\n228\tdef _fixture_all() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n229\t    return list(_FIXTURE.values())\n230\t\n231\t\n232\tdef _fixture_get(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n233\t    return _FIXTURE.get(key)\n234\t\n235\t\n236\tdef _fixture_for_code(code: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n237\t    code = (code or \"\").strip().upper()\n238\t    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if code in (p.get(\"related_codes\") or [])]\n239\t\n240\t\n241\tdef _fixture_for_job(job: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n242\t    job = (job or \"\").strip()\n243\t    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if job in (p.get(\"related_jobs\") or [])]\n244\t\n245\t\n246\t# --- torque resolution -------------------------------------------------------\n247\t\n248\tdef _resolve_torque(key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n249\t    \"\"\"One ``torque_keys`` entry resolved against the torque libraries.\n250\t\n251\t    Tries ``service_specs`` first, then ``drivetrain_specs`` -- the same\n252\t    order ``cuore.services.service_bridge`` implies by which module it\n253\t    reaches for which job. A key neither recognises still comes back as a\n254\t    row (UNKNOWN), never ``None`` -- a part card should be able to say\n255\t    \"no torque spec found for evap_esim_mount\" rather than silently drop it.\n256\t    \"\"\"\n257\t    for specs in (_service_specs(), _drivetrain_specs()):\n258\t        if specs is None:\n259\t            continue\n260\t        lookup = getattr(specs, \"torque_by_key\", None)\n261\t        if lookup is None:\n262\t            continue\n263\t        try:\n264\t            row = lookup(key)\n265\t        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a bad key must never 500 a part card\n266\t            row = None\n267\t        if row:\n268\t            return {\n269\t                \"key\": key,\n270\t                \"component\": row.get(\"component\"),\n271\t                \"value\": row.get(\"value\"),\n272\t                \"unit\": row.get(\"unit\"),\n273\t                \"display\": row.get(\"display\"),\n274\t                \"angle\": row.get(\"angle\"),\n275\t                \"single_use\": row.get(\"single_use\"),\n276\t                \"confidence\": row.get(\"confidence\", \"UNKNOWN\"),\n277\t                \"source\": row.get(\"source\"),\n278\t                \"notes\": row.get(\"notes\"),\n279\t            }\n280\t    return {\"key\": key, \"component\": None, \"value\": None, \"unit\": None,\n281\t            \"display\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"angle\": None, \"single_use\": False,\n282\t            \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None,\n283\t            \"notes\": \"no torque spec found for this key -- use the service manual (TechAuthority)\"}\n284\t\n285\t\n286\t_DEFAULTS: dict[str, Any] = {\n287\t    \"name\": \"\", \"what_it_does\": \"\", \"oem\": [], \"supersedes\": [],\n288\t    \"aftermarket\": [], \"fits\": \"\", \"location\": \"\", \"related_codes\": [],\n289\t    \"related_jobs\": [], \"torque_keys\": [], \"price\": None, \"buy\": [],\n290\t    \"images\": [], \"notes\": \"\",\n291\t}\n292\t\n293\t\n294\tdef _enrich(raw: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n295\t    \"\"\"Fill in any field the contract promises but a given row omits, and\n296\t    resolve ``torque_keys`` into a ``torques`` list of full spec rows.\"\"\"\n297\t    out = dict(_DEFAULTS)\n298\t    out.update(raw)\n299\t    out[\"torques\"] = [_resolve_torque(k) for k in (out.get(\"torque_keys\") or [])]\n300\t    return out\n301\t\n302\t\n303\t# --- public API ---------------------------------------------------------\n304\t\n305\tdef part(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n306\t    \"\"\"One part by key, enriched with resolved torques -- or ``None`` if no\n307\t    part by that key exists anywhere (real module or fixture).\n308\t\n309\t    ``mes.parts.get()`` returns the record without the key folded in (it's\n310\t    the dict key the caller already has); the fixture's own rows carry\n311\t    ``key`` already. Either way the result below always has it.\n312\t    \"\"\"\n313\t    if not key or not key.strip():\n314\t        return None\n315\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n316\t    try:\n317\t        raw = mod.get(key) if mod is not None else _fixture_get(key)\n318\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n319\t        raw = None\n320\t    if not raw:\n321\t        return None\n322\t    raw = {\"key\": key, **raw}\n323\t    return _enrich(raw)\n324\t\n325\t\n326\tdef _label_siblings(rows: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n327\t    for r in rows:\n328\t        sibling_of = r.get(\"sibling_of\")\n329\t        if sibling_of:\n330\t            r[\"label\"] = f\"from {str(sibling_of).title()} parts: verify fit\"\n331\t    return rows\n332\t\n333\t\n334\tdef parts_for_code(code: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n335\t    \"\"\"Every part related to a DTC -- ``[]`` if none are known, never an error.\n336\t\n337\t    ``vin``, if given, resolves a model via ``mes.platform.model_for_vin``\n338\t    and (only against the real ``mes.parts`` module, which supports it --\n339\t    the fixture does not) threads ``include_siblings=True`` through so any\n340\t    sourced sibling-platform part rows are included too, labeled \"from\n341\t    <Model> parts: verify fit\".\n342\t    \"\"\"\n343\t    if not code or not code.strip():\n344\t        return []\n345\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n346\t    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n347\t    try:\n348\t        if mod is not None:\n349\t            rows = mod.for_code(code, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n350\t        else:\n351\t            rows = _fixture_for_code(code)\n352\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n353\t        rows = []\n354\t    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n355\t\n356\t\n357\tdef parts_for_job(job: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n358\t    \"\"\"Every part related to a maintenance/service job -- ``[]`` if none.\n359\t    See :func:`parts_for_code` for ``vin``/``include_siblings`` behavior.\"\"\"\n360\t    if not job or not job.strip():\n361\t        return []\n362\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n363\t    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n364\t    try:\n365\t        if mod is not None:\n366\t            rows = mod.for_job(job, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n367\t        else:\n368\t            rows = _fixture_for_job(job)\n369\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n370\t        rows = []\n371\t    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n372\t\n373\t\n374\tdef all_parts() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n375\t    \"\"\"Every part known -- the backing list for the parts page's search box.\n376\t\n377\t    ``mes.parts.all()`` returns ``{key: record}`` (the key not folded into\n378\t    the record, same as ``get()``); the fixture's own ``_fixture_all()``\n379\t    already returns a list of rows each carrying ``key``.\n380\t    \"\"\"\n381\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n382\t    try:\n383\t        if mod is not None:\n384\t            rows = [{\"key\": k, **v} for k, v in mod.all().items()]\n385\t        else:\n386\t            rows = _fixture_all()\n387\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n388\t        rows = []\n389\t    return [_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])]\n390\t\n391\t\n392\tdef search_parts(q: str = \"\") -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n393\t    \"\"\"Case-insensitive substring match over name/key/what-it-does/OEM numbers.\"\"\"\n394\t    rows = all_parts()\n395\t    q = (q or \"\").strip().lower()\n396\t    if not q:\n397\t        return rows\n398\t    out = []\n399\t    for p in rows:\n400\t        haystack = \" \".join([\n401\t            p.get(\"key\", \"\"), p.get(\"name\", \"\"), p.get(\"what_it_does\", \"\"),\n402\t            \" \".join(o.get(\"number\", \"\") or \"\" for o in p.get(\"oem\", [])),\n403\t        ]).lower()\n404\t        if q in haystack:\n405\t            out.append(p)\n406\t    return out\n407\t\n408\t\n409\t__all__ = [\"part\", \"parts_for_code\", \"parts_for_job\", \"all_parts\", \"search_parts\"]\n410\t"}]},"uuid":"030e3a99-ba14-47ed-84d0-e1b0d6c7b416","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:09.034Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\parts_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"The only module in CUORE that imports :mod:`mes.parts`.\n\n``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` is being written in parallel by another agent\nand may not exist yet. Every call into it is wrapped and falls back to a\nbuilt-in fixture (shaped exactly like that module's documented contract --\nsee ``_FIXTURE`` below) so the parts page, the ``/api/parts*`` endpoints and\nthe part cards embedded in ``code.html``/``maintenance.html``/\n``oil_change.html``/``brakes_tires.html`` are developable and testable\nbefore it lands. Once ``mes.parts`` exists, nothing here needs to change --\nthe lazy import just starts succeeding and the fixture stops being reached.\n\nContract (``mes.parts``, once it lands): ``get(key)``, ``for_code(code)``,\n``for_job(job)``, ``all()``, each returning / each row shaped::\n\n    {key, name, what_it_does,\n     oem: [{number, brand, note, confidence, source}],\n     supersedes, aftermarket: [{brand, number, confidence, source}],\n     fits, location, related_codes, related_jobs, torque_keys,\n     price: {low, high, currency, as_of, source} | None,\n     buy: [{label, url}],\n     images: [{url, source_page, source_name, kind, licence_note, verified_at}],\n     notes}\n\n``torque_keys`` is a list of keys into the torque libraries -- resolved\nhere, not by ``mes.parts`` itself, against ``mes.service_specs`` and\n``mes.drivetrain_specs`` (the same two libraries\n``cuore.services.service_bridge`` already reaches through its own bridge),\nso a part card can show \"25 Nm, SINGLE-SOURCE\" without ``mes.parts`` needing\nto duplicate the torque library. A key neither library recognises resolves\nto an UNKNOWN row rather than being dropped, so the card can say so.\n\nEvery public function here degrades to an empty result (\"No part data yet\")\nrather than raising -- the one exception is :func:`part`, which returns\n``None`` for an unknown key so the API layer can turn that into a 404.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n\n\n# --- lazy imports, each independently guarded ------------------------------\n\ndef _parts_mod():\n    \"\"\"``mes.parts``, or ``None`` if it has not landed yet.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from mes import parts as parts_mod\n        return parts_mod\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- must never be why a page 500s\n        return None\n\n\ndef _service_specs():\n    try:\n        from mes import service_specs\n        return service_specs\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n\n\ndef _drivetrain_specs():\n    try:\n        from mes import drivetrain_specs\n        return drivetrain_specs\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n\n\ndef _model_for_vin(vin: Optional[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort model name for ``vin`` via ``mes.platform``, or ``None``\n    on any failure or an unrecognised VIN -- never raises.\"\"\"\n    if not vin:\n        return None\n    try:\n        from mes import platform as platform_mod\n        model = platform_mod.model_for_vin(vin)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n    return None if model == \"UNKNOWN\" else model\n\n\n# --- fixture: the exact shape mes.parts.get()/for_code()/for_job()/all()\n# will return, used until that module lands (or for any key it does not yet\n# cover). Keyed to things this corpus already knows about -- the Stelvio's\n# chronic P0455/P0456 EVAP family (see project_stelvio_evap.md) and the jobs\n# oil_change.html/maintenance.html/brakes_tires.html already render -- so a\n# developer working on those pages sees real-looking cards immediately. ----\n\n_FIXTURE: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {\n    \"esim\": {\n        \"key\": \"esim\",\n        \"name\": \"EVAP Service/Integrity Monitor (ESIM)\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Pressurizes the fuel-vapor system and watches the \"\n                        \"decay rate to detect small and large EVAP leaks. A \"\n                        \"failed self-test or a failed component sets \"\n                        \"P0455/P0456/P0457, not necessarily a leak itself.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68245527AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n                 \"note\": \"ESIM / natural-vacuum leak-detection pump assembly\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\"}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Standard Motor Products\", \"number\": \"EVAP1234\",\n                         \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Rear of the fuel tank, inline on the vapor line, ahead of the canister.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"P0457\"],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_esim_mount\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 180.0, \"high\": 260.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"},\n                {\"label\": \"Mopar eStore\", \"url\": \"https://www.moparonlineparts.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/data/esim-photo.jpg\",\n                    \"source_page\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\",\n                    \"source_name\": \"stelvioforum.com\", \"kind\": \"product_photo\",\n                    \"licence_note\": \"forum upload, fair-use reference only\",\n                    \"verified_at\": \"2026-09-20\"}],\n        \"notes\": \"Verified against TSB 18-030-17 before replacing -- that TSB's ECM \"\n                 \"calibration read fixes a false P0456 on some build dates without \"\n                 \"any part being replaced.\",\n    },\n    \"purge_valve\": {\n        \"key\": \"purge_valve\",\n        \"name\": \"EVAP Purge Solenoid Valve\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Opens under ECM control to let engine vacuum draw stored fuel \"\n                        \"vapor from the canister into the intake. Stuck closed or \"\n                        \"leaking, it can contribute to a P0455/P0456 decay-rate failure.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68093419AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n                 \"note\": \"Purge valve/solenoid\", \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n                 \"source\": \"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/purge-valve-location.9821/\"}],\n        \"supersedes\": [\"68093419A (earlier casting, same fit)\"],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Four Seasons\", \"number\": \"PV1029\",\n                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Intake manifold, driver's side, short hose run to the charcoal canister.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\"],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_purge_valve_mount\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 45.0, \"high\": 90.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"oil_filter\": {\n        \"key\": \"oil_filter\",\n        \"name\": \"Engine Oil Filter (cartridge element)\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Traps combustion byproducts and wear metal out of circulating oil.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68105175AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"cartridge element + housing cap\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/oil-change-maintenance-reset.19336/\"}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Mopar/Mann filter element\", \"number\": \"HU 711/51x\",\n                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T MultiAir (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Top of the engine, cartridge-style housing with a plastic cap.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"oil_change\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"filter_cap\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 18.0, \"high\": 32.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"engine_air_filter\": {\n        \"key\": \"engine_air_filter\",\n        \"name\": \"Engine Air Filter\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Keeps intake air clean of dust/debris ahead of the MAF/turbo.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68248729AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"panel element\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"K&N\", \"number\": \"33-5061\", \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n                         \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Airbox, passenger side of the engine bay.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"engine_air_filter\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [],\n        \"price\": None,\n        \"buy\": [],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"brake_pads_front\": {\n        \"key\": \"brake_pads_front\",\n        \"name\": \"Front Brake Pad Set\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Friction material clamped onto the front rotors by the caliper.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68273809AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"front pad set\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Brembo\", \"number\": \"P23165\", \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\",\n                         \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio, base brakes (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Front calipers.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"brakes_front\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"caliper_slider_front\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 90.0, \"high\": 160.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"wheel_lug_bolts\": {\n        \"key\": \"wheel_lug_bolts\",\n        \"name\": \"Wheel Lug Bolts\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Clamps the wheel to the hub.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68247068AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"lug bolt, M14\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Each wheel, five per corner.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"wheels\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"wheel_lug\"],\n        \"price\": None,\n        \"buy\": [],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n}\n\n\ndef _fixture_all() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    return list(_FIXTURE.values())\n\n\ndef _fixture_get(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    return _FIXTURE.get(key)\n\n\ndef _fixture_for_code(code: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    code = (code or \"\").strip().upper()\n    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if code in (p.get(\"related_codes\") or [])]\n\n\ndef _fixture_for_job(job: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    job = (job or \"\").strip()\n    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if job in (p.get(\"related_jobs\") or [])]\n\n\n# --- torque resolution -------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _resolve_torque(key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"One ``torque_keys`` entry resolved against the torque libraries.\n\n    Tries ``service_specs`` first, then ``drivetrain_specs`` -- the same\n    order ``cuore.services.service_bridge`` implies by which module it\n    reaches for which job. A key neither recognises still comes back as a\n    row (UNKNOWN), never ``None`` -- a part card should be able to say\n    \"no torque spec found for evap_esim_mount\" rather than silently drop it.\n    \"\"\"\n    for specs in (_service_specs(), _drivetrain_specs()):\n        if specs is None:\n            continue\n        lookup = getattr(specs, \"torque_by_key\", None)\n        if lookup is None:\n            continue\n        try:\n            row = lookup(key)\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a bad key must never 500 a part card\n            row = None\n        if row:\n            return {\n                \"key\": key,\n                \"component\": row.get(\"component\"),\n                \"value\": row.get(\"value\"),\n                \"unit\": row.get(\"unit\"),\n                \"display\": row.get(\"display\"),\n                \"angle\": row.get(\"angle\"),\n                \"single_use\": row.get(\"single_use\"),\n                \"confidence\": row.get(\"confidence\", \"UNKNOWN\"),\n                \"source\": row.get(\"source\"),\n                \"notes\": row.get(\"notes\"),\n            }\n    return {\"key\": key, \"component\": None, \"value\": None, \"unit\": None,\n            \"display\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"angle\": None, \"single_use\": False,\n            \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None,\n            \"notes\": \"no torque spec found for this key -- use the service manual (TechAuthority)\"}\n\n\n_DEFAULTS: dict[str, Any] = {\n    \"name\": \"\", \"what_it_does\": \"\", \"oem\": [], \"supersedes\": [],\n    \"aftermarket\": [], \"fits\": \"\", \"location\": \"\", \"related_codes\": [],\n    \"related_jobs\": [], \"torque_keys\": [], \"price\": None, \"buy\": [],\n    \"images\": [], \"notes\": \"\",\n}\n\n\ndef _enrich(raw: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Fill in any field the contract promises but a given row omits, and\n    resolve ``torque_keys`` into a ``torques`` list of full spec rows.\"\"\"\n    out = dict(_DEFAULTS)\n    out.update(raw)\n    out[\"torques\"] = [_resolve_torque(k) for k in (out.get(\"torque_keys\") or [])]\n    return out\n\n\n# --- public API ---------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef part(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"One part by key, enriched with resolved torques -- or ``None`` if no\n    part by that key exists anywhere (real module or fixture).\n\n    ``mes.parts.get()`` returns the record without the key folded in (it's\n    the dict key the caller already has); the fixture's own rows carry\n    ``key`` already. Either way the result below always has it.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not key or not key.strip():\n        return None\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    try:\n        raw = mod.get(key) if mod is not None else _fixture_get(key)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        raw = None\n    if not raw:\n        return None\n    raw = {\"key\": key, **raw}\n    return _enrich(raw)\n\n\ndef _label_siblings(rows: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    for r in rows:\n        sibling_of = r.get(\"sibling_of\")\n        if sibling_of:\n            r[\"label\"] = f\"from {str(sibling_of).title()} parts: verify fit\"\n    return rows\n\n\ndef parts_for_code(code: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every part related to a DTC -- ``[]`` if none are known, never an error.\n\n    ``vin``, if given, resolves a model via ``mes.platform.model_for_vin``\n    and (only against the real ``mes.parts`` module, which supports it --\n    the fixture does not) threads ``include_siblings=True`` through so any\n    sourced sibling-platform part rows are included too, labeled \"from\n    <Model> parts: verify fit\".\n    \"\"\"\n    if not code or not code.strip():\n        return []\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n    try:\n        if mod is not None:\n            rows = mod.for_code(code, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n        else:\n            rows = _fixture_for_code(code)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        rows = []\n    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n\n\ndef parts_for_job(job: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every part related to a maintenance/service job -- ``[]`` if none.\n    See :func:`parts_for_code` for ``vin``/``include_siblings`` behavior.\"\"\"\n    if not job or not job.strip():\n        return []\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n    try:\n        if mod is not None:\n            rows = mod.for_job(job, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n        else:\n            rows = _fixture_for_job(job)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        rows = []\n    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n\n\ndef all_parts() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every part known -- the backing list for the parts page's search box.\n\n    ``mes.parts.all()`` returns ``{key: record}`` (the key not folded into\n    the record, same as ``get()``); the fixture's own ``_fixture_all()``\n    already returns a list of rows each carrying ``key``.\n    \"\"\"\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    try:\n        if mod is not None:\n            rows = [{\"key\": k, **v} for k, v in mod.all().items()]\n        else:\n            rows = _fixture_all()\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        rows = []\n    return [_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])]\n\n\ndef search_parts(q: str = \"\") -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Case-insensitive substring match over name/key/what-it-does/OEM numbers.\"\"\"\n    rows = all_parts()\n    q = (q or \"\").strip().lower()\n    if not q:\n        return rows\n    out = []\n    for p in rows:\n        haystack = \" \".join([\n            p.get(\"key\", \"\"), p.get(\"name\", \"\"), p.get(\"what_it_does\", \"\"),\n            \" \".join(o.get(\"number\", \"\") or \"\" for o in p.get(\"oem\", [])),\n        ]).lower()\n        if q in haystack:\n            out.append(p)\n    return out\n\n\n__all__ = [\"part\", \"parts_for_code\", \"parts_for_job\", \"all_parts\", \"search_parts\"]\n","numLines":410,"startLine":1,"totalLines":410}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ce40408-c5fb-450e-83db-7995f230482a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"030e3a99-ba14-47ed-84d0-e1b0d6c7b416","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpyQmn1GFPsd4cJjs53b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AwLjipg3qAyDZkSgn3SJwA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\tools_kb_bridge.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16504,"cache_read_input_tokens":82918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16504,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AwLjipg3qAyDZkSgn3SJwA":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\tools_kb_bridge.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f78b0ee6-3100-4f3c-be9c-92c14033f6bb","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfpyQmUQWxgKYX93bWBni","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fe78ec7-741e-4334-bc21-cdc101718892","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:09.551Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"6fe78ec7-741e-4334-bc21-cdc101718892","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8683b5a-1bb3-40f7-aff9-33655508a2e2","agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AwLjipg3qAyDZkSgn3SJwA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"HTTP/template face of :mod:`mes.tools_kb` and :mod:`mes.tool_usage`.\n2\t\n3\tSame posture as ``cuore.services.feedback_bridge``: a thin bridge that\n4\ttranslates ``mes``'s own ``ValueError``s into :class:`BadRequest`, used by\n5\tboth ``cuore/api/tools_kb.py`` (JSON) and the Jinja globals registered in\n6\t``cuore/web/tools_kb_globals.py`` (for ``job.html``/``maintenance.html``).\n7\t\n8\tNothing here invents a tool, a size, or a verdict -- ``recommend`` and\n9\t``learn`` are direct pass-through reads; the only shaping done here is\n10\tmerging a step's recommendation with what was actually learned about it\n11\t(:func:`recommend_with_learning`), so the Job page's \"Tools for this step\"\n12\tpanel can show both in one call.\n13\t\"\"\"\n14\t\n15\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n16\t\n17\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n18\t\n19\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n20\tfrom .errors import BadRequest\n21\t\n22\tfrom mes import tool_usage as tool_usage_mod  # noqa: E402\n23\tfrom mes import tools_kb  # noqa: E402\n24\t\n25\t\n26\tdef recommend(step: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n27\t    \"\"\"Tool rows for one job/step key -- see ``mes.tools_kb.recommend`` --\n28\t    each annotated with ``have`` (\"owned\"/\"not_owned\"/\"unknown\", from the\n29\t    garage's own simple inventory list) and, for a *required* tool that\n30\t    isn't owned, a ``decision`` card (see ``mes.tools_kb.decision_for``) --\n31\t    one worked example exists (the EVAP smoke machine), everything else\n32\t    returns ``None`` and the UI shows no card.\"\"\"\n33\t    step = (step or \"\").strip()\n34\t    rows = tools_kb.recommend(step)\n35\t    for row in rows:\n36\t        key = row[\"tool_info\"][\"key\"]\n37\t        have = tool_usage_mod.have_status(key)\n38\t        row[\"have\"] = have\n39\t        row[\"decision\"] = (tools_kb.decision_for(step, key)\n40\t                           if row[\"required\"] and have != \"owned\" else None)\n41\t    return rows\n42\t\n43\t\n44\tdef learn(step: str, *, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n45\t    \"\"\"Aggregated learning for one job/step key -- see ``mes.tool_usage.learn``.\"\"\"\n46\t    return tool_usage_mod.learn(step, vin=vin)\n47\t\n48\t\n49\tdef recommend_with_learning(step: str, *, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n50\t    \"\"\"What the Job/Maintenance pages actually need for one step: the\n51\t    recommended tools, plus what was learned about this step last time\n52\t    (top tools used, flagged wrong, buy suggestions, missing tools) --\n53\t    scoped to this VIN first, falling back to every vehicle.\"\"\"\n54\t    step = (step or \"\").strip()\n55\t    return {\n56\t        \"step\": step,\n57\t        \"tools\": recommend(step),\n58\t        \"learned\": learn(step, vin=vin),\n59\t    }\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tdef add_usage(vin: str, step: str, *, job_id: str = \"\", by: str = \"\",\n63\t             tools_used: Optional[list[dict[str, Any]]] = None,\n64\t             missing_tools: Optional[list[str]] = None,\n65\t             would_buy: Optional[list[dict[str, Any]]] = None,\n66\t             time_min: Optional[float] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n67\t    \"\"\"Record one tool-usage review. Raises BadRequest on invalid input.\"\"\"\n68\t    try:\n69\t        return tool_usage_mod.add(vin, step, job_id=job_id, by=by, tools_used=tools_used,\n70\t                                  missing_tools=missing_tools, would_buy=would_buy,\n71\t                                  time_min=time_min)\n72\t    except ValueError as exc:\n73\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n74\t\n75\t\n76\tdef usage_for(vin: str, *, step: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n77\t    \"\"\"Every tool-usage review recorded for this VIN, optionally filtered\n78\t    by step -- oldest first.\"\"\"\n79\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n80\t    if not vin:\n81\t        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n82\t    return tool_usage_mod.load(vin=vin, step=step)\n83\t\n84\t\n85\tdef has_review(vin: str, job_id: str) -> bool:\n86\t    \"\"\"Whether any tool-usage review has been recorded against this job --\n87\t    the gate ``cuore.web.jobs_routes`` checks before letting a job close.\"\"\"\n88\t    if not job_id:\n89\t        return False\n90\t    return any(r.get(\"job_id\") == job_id for r in tool_usage_mod.load(vin=vin))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\tdef inventory_set(tool: str, status: str, *, note: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n94\t    \"\"\"Record whether the shop has this tool -- \"owned\"/\"not_owned\".\n95\t    Raises BadRequest on invalid input.\"\"\"\n96\t    try:\n97\t        return tool_usage_mod.inventory_set(tool, status, note=note)\n98\t    except ValueError as exc:\n99\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n100\t\n101\t\n102\tdef inventory_list() -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n103\t    \"\"\"The garage's current owned/not-owned list, keyed by tool.\"\"\"\n104\t    return tool_usage_mod.inventory_list()\n105\t\n106\t\n107\t__all__ = [\"recommend\", \"learn\", \"recommend_with_learning\", \"add_usage\",\n108\t          \"usage_for\", \"has_review\", \"inventory_set\", \"inventory_list\"]\n109\t"}]},"uuid":"de91781c-85ab-43b4-bee4-554ad1e27760","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:09.572Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\tools_kb_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"HTTP/template face of :mod:`mes.tools_kb` and :mod:`mes.tool_usage`.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore.services.feedback_bridge``: a thin bridge that\ntranslates ``mes``'s own ``ValueError``s into :class:`BadRequest`, used by\nboth ``cuore/api/tools_kb.py`` (JSON) and the Jinja globals registered in\n``cuore/web/tools_kb_globals.py`` (for ``job.html``/``maintenance.html``).\n\nNothing here invents a tool, a size, or a verdict -- ``recommend`` and\n``learn`` are direct pass-through reads; the only shaping done here is\nmerging a step's recommendation with what was actually learned about it\n(:func:`recommend_with_learning`), so the Job page's \"Tools for this step\"\npanel can show both in one call.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom .errors import BadRequest\n\nfrom mes import tool_usage as tool_usage_mod  # noqa: E402\nfrom mes import tools_kb  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef recommend(step: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Tool rows for one job/step key -- see ``mes.tools_kb.recommend`` --\n    each annotated with ``have`` (\"owned\"/\"not_owned\"/\"unknown\", from the\n    garage's own simple inventory list) and, for a *required* tool that\n    isn't owned, a ``decision`` card (see ``mes.tools_kb.decision_for``) --\n    one worked example exists (the EVAP smoke machine), everything else\n    returns ``None`` and the UI shows no card.\"\"\"\n    step = (step or \"\").strip()\n    rows = tools_kb.recommend(step)\n    for row in rows:\n        key = row[\"tool_info\"][\"key\"]\n        have = tool_usage_mod.have_status(key)\n        row[\"have\"] = have\n        row[\"decision\"] = (tools_kb.decision_for(step, key)\n                           if row[\"required\"] and have != \"owned\" else None)\n    return rows\n\n\ndef learn(step: str, *, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Aggregated learning for one job/step key -- see ``mes.tool_usage.learn``.\"\"\"\n    return tool_usage_mod.learn(step, vin=vin)\n\n\ndef recommend_with_learning(step: str, *, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"What the Job/Maintenance pages actually need for one step: the\n    recommended tools, plus what was learned about this step last time\n    (top tools used, flagged wrong, buy suggestions, missing tools) --\n    scoped to this VIN first, falling back to every vehicle.\"\"\"\n    step = (step or \"\").strip()\n    return {\n        \"step\": step,\n        \"tools\": recommend(step),\n        \"learned\": learn(step, vin=vin),\n    }\n\n\ndef add_usage(vin: str, step: str, *, job_id: str = \"\", by: str = \"\",\n             tools_used: Optional[list[dict[str, Any]]] = None,\n             missing_tools: Optional[list[str]] = None,\n             would_buy: Optional[list[dict[str, Any]]] = None,\n             time_min: Optional[float] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Record one tool-usage review. Raises BadRequest on invalid input.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return tool_usage_mod.add(vin, step, job_id=job_id, by=by, tools_used=tools_used,\n                                  missing_tools=missing_tools, would_buy=would_buy,\n                                  time_min=time_min)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef usage_for(vin: str, *, step: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every tool-usage review recorded for this VIN, optionally filtered\n    by step -- oldest first.\"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n    return tool_usage_mod.load(vin=vin, step=step)\n\n\ndef has_review(vin: str, job_id: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether any tool-usage review has been recorded against this job --\n    the gate ``cuore.web.jobs_routes`` checks before letting a job close.\"\"\"\n    if not job_id:\n        return False\n    return any(r.get(\"job_id\") == job_id for r in tool_usage_mod.load(vin=vin))\n\n\ndef inventory_set(tool: str, status: str, *, note: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Record whether the shop has this tool -- \"owned\"/\"not_owned\".\n    Raises BadRequest on invalid input.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return tool_usage_mod.inventory_set(tool, status, note=note)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef inventory_list() -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"The garage's current owned/not-owned list, keyed by tool.\"\"\"\n    return tool_usage_mod.inventory_list()\n\n\n__all__ = [\"recommend\", \"learn\", \"recommend_with_learning\", \"add_usage\",\n          \"usage_for\", \"has_review\", \"inventory_set\", \"inventory_list\"]\n","numLines":109,"startLine":1,"totalLines":109}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6fe78ec7-741e-4334-bc21-cdc101718892","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"de91781c-85ab-43b4-bee4-554ad1e27760","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpyQmn1GFPsd4cJjs53b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011U559mq8vk4ykYjjjJgztK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\shop_bridge.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16504,"cache_read_input_tokens":82918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16504,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011U559mq8vk4ykYjjjJgztK":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\shop_bridge.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f78b0ee6-3100-4f3c-be9c-92c14033f6bb","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CfpyQmUQWxgKYX93bWBni","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3de9f06-9a59-4c58-a49f-1b4dc9d09c18","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:10.019Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c3de9f06-9a59-4c58-a49f-1b4dc9d09c18","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8683b5a-1bb3-40f7-aff9-33655508a2e2","agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011U559mq8vk4ykYjjjJgztK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Assembles the one-car-at-a-time shop pages: ``/start`` and the release\n2\tgate.\n3\t\n4\tSame posture as ``cuore.services.jobs_bridge``: this is the only module\n5\tbesides ``jobs_bridge`` that imports :mod:`mes.shop` directly. Writing\n6\t(intake, step timing, release) is thin pass-through to :mod:`mes.shop`,\n7\twhich does the validation; reading enriches the raw visit with the\n8\tvehicle's name (from the corpus, via ``mes_bridge``) and the dossier's\n9\tverdict (via ``dossier_bridge``), so the release gate can show the evidence\n10\tbehind \"verified\" instead of trusting a mechanic's checkbox.\n11\t\"\"\"\n12\t\n13\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n14\t\n15\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n16\t\n17\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n18\tfrom . import dossier_bridge, mes_bridge\n19\tfrom .errors import BadRequest, NotFound\n20\t\n21\tfrom mes import shop as shop_mod  # noqa: E402\n22\t\n23\ttry:\n24\t    from . import jobs_bridge\n25\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the release page must still render\n26\t    jobs_bridge = None\n27\t\n28\ttry:\n29\t    from mes import tool_usage as tool_usage_mod\n30\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the tools-away section must still render\n31\t    tool_usage_mod = None\n32\t\n33\t\n34\t# --- vehicle name lookup, for intake prefill and board display -------------\n35\t\n36\t#: WMI (VIN positions 1-4) -> make, for the handful of makes this shop\n37\t#: actually sees. Decoding stops at \"make\" -- the model is deliberately\n38\t#: reported as \"UNKNOWN\" rather than guessed from trim/engine codes nobody\n39\t#: has mapped yet.\n40\t_WMI_MAKES: dict[str, str] = {\n41\t    \"ZASF\": \"Alfa Romeo\",\n42\t    \"ZN6\": \"Maserati\",\n43\t    \"ZN7\": \"Maserati\",\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t\n47\tdef vehicle_choices() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n48\t    \"\"\"VIN + display name for every real vehicle in the corpus, for the\n49\t    intake form's VIN prefill.\"\"\"\n50\t    try:\n51\t        found = mes_bridge.vehicles(real_only=True)\n52\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n53\t        return []\n54\t    return [{\"vin\": v.get(\"vin\", \"\"),\n55\t            \"name\": (v.get(\"names\") or [\"\"])[0] or v.get(\"vin\", \"\")}\n56\t           for v in found if v.get(\"vin\")]\n57\t\n58\t\n59\tdef _vehicle_name(vin: str) -> str:\n60\t    \"\"\"The corpus's own name for this VIN, from the vehicle list -- empty\n61\t    when this VIN is not (yet) one of the corpus's known vehicles.\"\"\"\n62\t    for v in vehicle_choices():\n63\t        if v[\"vin\"] == vin:\n64\t            return v[\"name\"]\n65\t    return \"\"\n66\t\n67\t\n68\tdef _decode_wmi(vin: str) -> str:\n69\t    \"\"\"Make only, from the VIN's WMI -- longest-prefix match so a 4-char\n70\t    WMI (``ZASF``) is tried before a 3-char one (``ZN6``/``ZN7``) that could\n71\t    otherwise shadow it. ``\"\"`` when the WMI is not one this shop knows.\"\"\"\n72\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip().upper()\n73\t    for prefix in sorted(_WMI_MAKES, key=len, reverse=True):\n74\t        if vin.startswith(prefix):\n75\t            return _WMI_MAKES[prefix]\n76\t    return \"\"\n77\t\n78\t\n79\tdef resolve_vehicle_name(vin: str) -> str:\n80\t    \"\"\"Best name available for this VIN at the moment a visit/job is\n81\t    created, so a car with no name on file yet is never shown as\n82\t    \"(unnamed vehicle)\": the corpus's own vehicle list, then the dossier\n83\t    identity's own ``vehicle`` field (:func:`mes_bridge.workup`), then a WMI\n84\t    decode (make only, model \"UNKNOWN\"), then -- if nothing resolves at all\n85\t    -- the VIN itself, since a known VIN must never render as unnamed.\"\"\"\n86\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n87\t    if not vin:\n88\t        return \"\"\n89\t    name = _vehicle_name(vin)\n90\t    if name:\n91\t        return name\n92\t    try:\n93\t        identity = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin).get(\"identity\") or {}\n94\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n95\t        identity = {}\n96\t    if identity.get(\"vehicle\"):\n97\t        return identity[\"vehicle\"]\n98\t    make = _decode_wmi(vin)\n99\t    if make:\n100\t        return f\"{make} UNKNOWN\"\n101\t    return vin\n102\t\n103\t\n104\t# --- write surface, thin pass-through to mes.shop ---------------------------\n105\t\n106\t\n107\tdef intake(vin: str, complaint: str = \"\", *, technician: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n108\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n109\t    if not vin:\n110\t        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n111\t    try:\n112\t        return shop_mod.intake(vin, complaint, technician=technician,\n113\t                               vehicle=resolve_vehicle_name(vin))\n114\t    except ValueError as exc:\n115\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n116\t\n117\t\n118\tdef start_step(visit_id: str, step: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n119\t    try:\n120\t        return shop_mod.start_step(visit_id, step)\n121\t    except ValueError as exc:\n122\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n123\t\n124\t\n125\tdef end_step(visit_id: str, step: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n126\t    try:\n127\t        return shop_mod.end_step(visit_id, step)\n128\t    except ValueError as exc:\n129\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n130\t\n131\t\n132\tdef release(visit_id: str, checks: dict[str, Any], *,\n133\t           reason: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n134\t    \"\"\"Release the car. ``verified`` is never taken from ``checks`` -- it is\n135\t    looked up fresh from this visit's dossier verdict here, so a mechanic\n136\t    cannot tick a box into verification; only a ``VERIFIED_CLEAN`` dossier\n137\t    does that. Never blocks: this just records the decision.\"\"\"\n138\t    visit = get_visit(visit_id)\n139\t    dossier_verified = _dossier_verdict(visit[\"vin\"]).get(\"state\") == \"VERIFIED_CLEAN\"\n140\t    try:\n141\t        return shop_mod.release(visit_id, checks, dossier_verified=dossier_verified,\n142\t                                reason=reason)\n143\t    except ValueError as exc:\n144\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n145\t\n146\t\n147\tdef get_visit(visit_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n148\t    visit = shop_mod.get(visit_id)\n149\t    if visit is None:\n150\t        raise NotFound(f\"no visit {visit_id!r}\")\n151\t    return visit\n152\t\n153\t\n154\tdef current_visit_for_vin(vin: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n155\t    \"\"\"The visit a mechanic walking up to this car right now would be\n156\t    working on: the newest not-out visit, or (if every visit for this VIN\n157\t    has already gone out) the most recent one -- so ``/v/{vin}/release``\n158\t    still has something to show for a car that was already released today.\"\"\"\n159\t    visit = shop_mod.current(vin)\n160\t    if visit is not None:\n161\t        return visit\n162\t    visits = shop_mod.load(vin)\n163\t    return visits[-1] if visits else None\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t# --- reads -------------------------------------------------------------------\n167\t\n168\t\n169\tdef _tool_review(job_id: Optional[str]) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n170\t    \"\"\"The Job's tool review, if ``jobs_bridge`` (or the job record itself)\n171\t    ever exposes one. Nothing in this corpus currently writes a tool review,\n172\t    so this returns ``None`` -- the release page shows \"not reviewed\" rather\n173\t    than inventing a result.\"\"\"\n174\t    if not job_id or jobs_bridge is None:\n175\t        return None\n176\t    getter = getattr(jobs_bridge, \"tool_review\", None)\n177\t    if callable(getter):\n178\t        try:\n179\t            return getter(job_id)\n180\t        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n181\t            return None\n182\t    try:\n183\t        job = jobs_bridge.get_job(job_id)\n184\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n185\t        return None\n186\t    return job.get(\"tool_review\") if isinstance(job, dict) else None\n187\t\n188\t\n189\tdef tools_used_for_visit(vin: str, job_id: Optional[str]) -> list[str]:\n190\t    \"\"\"Distinct tool names from this car's tools-used review\n191\t    (:mod:`mes.tool_usage`), for the release page's \"Tools away\" checklist.\n192\t    ``[]`` when that module is not installed yet or has nothing on file --\n193\t    the section still renders, just with nothing to tick.\"\"\"\n194\t    if tool_usage_mod is None:\n195\t        return []\n196\t    try:\n197\t        rows = tool_usage_mod.load(vin=vin)\n198\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n199\t        return []\n200\t    seen: set[str] = set()\n201\t    names: list[str] = []\n202\t    for r in rows:\n203\t        if job_id and r.get(\"job_id\") and r.get(\"job_id\") != job_id:\n204\t            continue\n205\t        for t in r.get(\"tools_used\", []) or []:\n206\t            name = t.get(\"tool\") if isinstance(t, dict) else None\n207\t            if name and name not in seen:\n208\t                seen.add(name)\n209\t                names.append(name)\n210\t    return names\n211\t\n212\t\n213\tdef confirm_tools_away(vin: str, job_id: Optional[str], put_away: list[dict[str, Any]],\n214\t                       restock: str, not_available: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> bool:\n215\t    \"\"\"Record the mechanic's tools-away confirmation via\n216\t    ``mes.tool_usage.tools_away`` if that function exists yet -- advise,\n217\t    never block: any failure, or the function simply not existing on this\n218\t    install, must never stop the mechanic moving to the next car. Returns\n219\t    whether the confirmation was actually recorded.\"\"\"\n220\t    if tool_usage_mod is None:\n221\t        return False\n222\t    fn = getattr(tool_usage_mod, \"tools_away\", None)\n223\t    if not callable(fn):\n224\t        return False\n225\t    try:\n226\t        fn(vin, job_id or \"\", put_away=put_away, restock=restock,\n227\t          not_available=not_available)\n228\t        return True\n229\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n230\t        return False\n231\t\n232\t\n233\tdef build_release_view(visit_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n234\t    \"\"\"Everything the release gate needs: the visit, its dossier verdict (so\n235\t    an UNVERIFIED car is flagged before release, not after), and whatever\n236\t    tool review the Job carries.\"\"\"\n237\t    visit = get_visit(visit_id)\n238\t    return _release_view_for(visit)\n239\t\n240\t\n241\tdef build_release_view_for_vin(vin: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n242\t    \"\"\"Same as :func:`build_release_view`, resolved from a VIN instead of a\n243\t    visit id -- what ``/v/{vin}/release`` renders.\"\"\"\n244\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n245\t    if not vin:\n246\t        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n247\t    visit = current_visit_for_vin(vin)\n248\t    if visit is None:\n249\t        raise NotFound(f\"no shop visit on record for {vin!r}\")\n250\t    return _release_view_for(visit)\n251\t\n252\t\n253\tdef _dossier_verdict(vin: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n254\t    \"\"\"This VIN's dossier verdict, or ``{}`` when it cannot be computed --\n255\t    never raises, since both the release decision and the release page must\n256\t    still work when the dossier is unavailable (then treated as not\n257\t    verified, the safer default).\"\"\"\n258\t    try:\n259\t        dossier = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin)\n260\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n261\t        return {}\n262\t    try:\n263\t        return dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, None).get(\"verdict\") or {}\n264\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n265\t        return {}\n266\t\n267\t\n268\tdef _release_view_for(visit: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n269\t    vin = visit[\"vin\"]\n270\t    verdict = _dossier_verdict(vin)\n271\t    return {\n272\t        \"visit\": visit,\n273\t        \"vin\": vin,\n274\t        \"dossier_verdict\": verdict or None,\n275\t        \"verified\": verdict.get(\"state\") == \"VERIFIED_CLEAN\",\n276\t        \"tool_review\": _tool_review(visit.get(\"job_id\")),\n277\t        \"tools_used\": tools_used_for_visit(vin, visit.get(\"job_id\")),\n278\t        \"checks\": list(shop_mod.RELEASE_CHECKS),\n279\t    }\n280\t\n281\t\n282\t__all__ = [\"vehicle_choices\", \"resolve_vehicle_name\", \"intake\", \"start_step\", \"end_step\",\n283\t          \"release\", \"get_visit\", \"build_release_view\",\n284\t          \"build_release_view_for_vin\", \"current_visit_for_vin\",\n285\t          \"tools_used_for_visit\", \"confirm_tools_away\"]\n286\t"}]},"uuid":"0a78dff8-0947-4d04-b67a-e894e2248f55","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:10.040Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\shop_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"Assembles the one-car-at-a-time shop pages: ``/start`` and the release\ngate.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore.services.jobs_bridge``: this is the only module\nbesides ``jobs_bridge`` that imports :mod:`mes.shop` directly. Writing\n(intake, step timing, release) is thin pass-through to :mod:`mes.shop`,\nwhich does the validation; reading enriches the raw visit with the\nvehicle's name (from the corpus, via ``mes_bridge``) and the dossier's\nverdict (via ``dossier_bridge``), so the release gate can show the evidence\nbehind \"verified\" instead of trusting a mechanic's checkbox.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom . import dossier_bridge, mes_bridge\nfrom .errors import BadRequest, NotFound\n\nfrom mes import shop as shop_mod  # noqa: E402\n\ntry:\n    from . import jobs_bridge\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the release page must still render\n    jobs_bridge = None\n\ntry:\n    from mes import tool_usage as tool_usage_mod\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the tools-away section must still render\n    tool_usage_mod = None\n\n\n# --- vehicle name lookup, for intake prefill and board display -------------\n\n#: WMI (VIN positions 1-4) -> make, for the handful of makes this shop\n#: actually sees. Decoding stops at \"make\" -- the model is deliberately\n#: reported as \"UNKNOWN\" rather than guessed from trim/engine codes nobody\n#: has mapped yet.\n_WMI_MAKES: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"ZASF\": \"Alfa Romeo\",\n    \"ZN6\": \"Maserati\",\n    \"ZN7\": \"Maserati\",\n}\n\n\ndef vehicle_choices() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"VIN + display name for every real vehicle in the corpus, for the\n    intake form's VIN prefill.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        found = mes_bridge.vehicles(real_only=True)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return []\n    return [{\"vin\": v.get(\"vin\", \"\"),\n            \"name\": (v.get(\"names\") or [\"\"])[0] or v.get(\"vin\", \"\")}\n           for v in found if v.get(\"vin\")]\n\n\ndef _vehicle_name(vin: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The corpus's own name for this VIN, from the vehicle list -- empty\n    when this VIN is not (yet) one of the corpus's known vehicles.\"\"\"\n    for v in vehicle_choices():\n        if v[\"vin\"] == vin:\n            return v[\"name\"]\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef _decode_wmi(vin: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Make only, from the VIN's WMI -- longest-prefix match so a 4-char\n    WMI (``ZASF``) is tried before a 3-char one (``ZN6``/``ZN7``) that could\n    otherwise shadow it. ``\"\"`` when the WMI is not one this shop knows.\"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip().upper()\n    for prefix in sorted(_WMI_MAKES, key=len, reverse=True):\n        if vin.startswith(prefix):\n            return _WMI_MAKES[prefix]\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef resolve_vehicle_name(vin: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best name available for this VIN at the moment a visit/job is\n    created, so a car with no name on file yet is never shown as\n    \"(unnamed vehicle)\": the corpus's own vehicle list, then the dossier\n    identity's own ``vehicle`` field (:func:`mes_bridge.workup`), then a WMI\n    decode (make only, model \"UNKNOWN\"), then -- if nothing resolves at all\n    -- the VIN itself, since a known VIN must never render as unnamed.\"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        return \"\"\n    name = _vehicle_name(vin)\n    if name:\n        return name\n    try:\n        identity = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin).get(\"identity\") or {}\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        identity = {}\n    if identity.get(\"vehicle\"):\n        return identity[\"vehicle\"]\n    make = _decode_wmi(vin)\n    if make:\n        return f\"{make} UNKNOWN\"\n    return vin\n\n\n# --- write surface, thin pass-through to mes.shop ---------------------------\n\n\ndef intake(vin: str, complaint: str = \"\", *, technician: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n    try:\n        return shop_mod.intake(vin, complaint, technician=technician,\n                               vehicle=resolve_vehicle_name(vin))\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef start_step(visit_id: str, step: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    try:\n        return shop_mod.start_step(visit_id, step)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef end_step(visit_id: str, step: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    try:\n        return shop_mod.end_step(visit_id, step)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef release(visit_id: str, checks: dict[str, Any], *,\n           reason: Optional[str] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Release the car. ``verified`` is never taken from ``checks`` -- it is\n    looked up fresh from this visit's dossier verdict here, so a mechanic\n    cannot tick a box into verification; only a ``VERIFIED_CLEAN`` dossier\n    does that. Never blocks: this just records the decision.\"\"\"\n    visit = get_visit(visit_id)\n    dossier_verified = _dossier_verdict(visit[\"vin\"]).get(\"state\") == \"VERIFIED_CLEAN\"\n    try:\n        return shop_mod.release(visit_id, checks, dossier_verified=dossier_verified,\n                                reason=reason)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef get_visit(visit_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    visit = shop_mod.get(visit_id)\n    if visit is None:\n        raise NotFound(f\"no visit {visit_id!r}\")\n    return visit\n\n\ndef current_visit_for_vin(vin: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"The visit a mechanic walking up to this car right now would be\n    working on: the newest not-out visit, or (if every visit for this VIN\n    has already gone out) the most recent one -- so ``/v/{vin}/release``\n    still has something to show for a car that was already released today.\"\"\"\n    visit = shop_mod.current(vin)\n    if visit is not None:\n        return visit\n    visits = shop_mod.load(vin)\n    return visits[-1] if visits else None\n\n\n# --- reads -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _tool_review(job_id: Optional[str]) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"The Job's tool review, if ``jobs_bridge`` (or the job record itself)\n    ever exposes one. Nothing in this corpus currently writes a tool review,\n    so this returns ``None`` -- the release page shows \"not reviewed\" rather\n    than inventing a result.\"\"\"\n    if not job_id or jobs_bridge is None:\n        return None\n    getter = getattr(jobs_bridge, \"tool_review\", None)\n    if callable(getter):\n        try:\n            return getter(job_id)\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n            return None\n    try:\n        job = jobs_bridge.get_job(job_id)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n    return job.get(\"tool_review\") if isinstance(job, dict) else None\n\n\ndef tools_used_for_visit(vin: str, job_id: Optional[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Distinct tool names from this car's tools-used review\n    (:mod:`mes.tool_usage`), for the release page's \"Tools away\" checklist.\n    ``[]`` when that module is not installed yet or has nothing on file --\n    the section still renders, just with nothing to tick.\"\"\"\n    if tool_usage_mod is None:\n        return []\n    try:\n        rows = tool_usage_mod.load(vin=vin)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return []\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    names: list[str] = []\n    for r in rows:\n        if job_id and r.get(\"job_id\") and r.get(\"job_id\") != job_id:\n            continue\n        for t in r.get(\"tools_used\", []) or []:\n            name = t.get(\"tool\") if isinstance(t, dict) else None\n            if name and name not in seen:\n                seen.add(name)\n                names.append(name)\n    return names\n\n\ndef confirm_tools_away(vin: str, job_id: Optional[str], put_away: list[dict[str, Any]],\n                       restock: str, not_available: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Record the mechanic's tools-away confirmation via\n    ``mes.tool_usage.tools_away`` if that function exists yet -- advise,\n    never block: any failure, or the function simply not existing on this\n    install, must never stop the mechanic moving to the next car. Returns\n    whether the confirmation was actually recorded.\"\"\"\n    if tool_usage_mod is None:\n        return False\n    fn = getattr(tool_usage_mod, \"tools_away\", None)\n    if not callable(fn):\n        return False\n    try:\n        fn(vin, job_id or \"\", put_away=put_away, restock=restock,\n          not_available=not_available)\n        return True\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return False\n\n\ndef build_release_view(visit_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Everything the release gate needs: the visit, its dossier verdict (so\n    an UNVERIFIED car is flagged before release, not after), and whatever\n    tool review the Job carries.\"\"\"\n    visit = get_visit(visit_id)\n    return _release_view_for(visit)\n\n\ndef build_release_view_for_vin(vin: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Same as :func:`build_release_view`, resolved from a VIN instead of a\n    visit id -- what ``/v/{vin}/release`` renders.\"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n    visit = current_visit_for_vin(vin)\n    if visit is None:\n        raise NotFound(f\"no shop visit on record for {vin!r}\")\n    return _release_view_for(visit)\n\n\ndef _dossier_verdict(vin: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"This VIN's dossier verdict, or ``{}`` when it cannot be computed --\n    never raises, since both the release decision and the release page must\n    still work when the dossier is unavailable (then treated as not\n    verified, the safer default).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        dossier = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return {}\n    try:\n        return dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, None).get(\"verdict\") or {}\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return {}\n\n\ndef _release_view_for(visit: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    vin = visit[\"vin\"]\n    verdict = _dossier_verdict(vin)\n    return {\n        \"visit\": visit,\n        \"vin\": vin,\n        \"dossier_verdict\": verdict or None,\n        \"verified\": verdict.get(\"state\") == \"VERIFIED_CLEAN\",\n        \"tool_review\": _tool_review(visit.get(\"job_id\")),\n        \"tools_used\": tools_used_for_visit(vin, visit.get(\"job_id\")),\n        \"checks\": list(shop_mod.RELEASE_CHECKS),\n    }\n\n\n__all__ = [\"vehicle_choices\", \"resolve_vehicle_name\", \"intake\", \"start_step\", \"end_step\",\n          \"release\", \"get_visit\", \"build_release_view\",\n          \"build_release_view_for_vin\", \"current_visit_for_vin\",\n          \"tools_used_for_visit\", \"confirm_tools_away\"]\n","numLines":286,"startLine":1,"totalLines":286}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3de9f06-9a59-4c58-a49f-1b4dc9d09c18","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
