{"parentUuid":"1b570263-6703-48af-a78c-1227f75a2ca4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aed09da2792eef1c4","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfq1tABsj2ML1KXHF2Crj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CDMwUnsKnDfQowNTZkHLf9","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Bench page built and wired end-to-end; all 4 requested tests pass (check_bench.py 39/39, check_dossier_page.py 42/42, check_dossier_view.py 35/35, check_api.py 96/96 green).\n\nFiles created:\n- cuore/services/bench_bridge.py — build_bench(vin): vehicle name (never unnamed), vin_tail, km, complaint, verdict {state,label,sentence,next_action,blocker}, next_actions (top 3 unchecked steps, ACTIVE families first, each with parts/tools/bulletin/href_tick), open_codes_count, last_read, shortcuts (max 6), case_hint.\n- cuore/web/bench_routes.py — new router, GET /v/{vin} renders bench.html via bench_bridge; reuses the existing POST /v/{vin}/checklist form.\n- cuore/web/templates/bench.html — no hero/step bar, scoped <style> only (cuore.css untouched): 40px status line (name/VIN tail/km/verdict chip) in the vehiclebar block, next_action sentence at 20px, up to 3 big action cards (44px tick button, bulletin chip, parts line, tools w/ have-status), shortcut chips, Job/Full dossier links.\n- cuore/tests/check_bench.py — 5 checks incl. one 400px CDP screenshot (cleanup via _edge_cleanup.kill_edge_profile).\n\nFiles edited:\n- cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py — added verdict.next_action/blocker/next_step_id only, computed in build_view from the existing verdict state, open-work order, and freeze-frame fuel flag (no new judgement, just composes what was already there).\n- cuore/web/routes.py — GET /v/{vin} moved to GET /v/{vin}/dossier (tab stays \"dossier\"); updated module docstring's page table; notes-form redirect updated to the new path.\n- cuore/app.py — registered bench_routes.router (included right after web_routes.router so it claims /v/{vin} now that routes.py no longer does).\n- cuore/web/i18n.py — added full_dossier/mark_done/nothing_open/have_it/need_it (en+it).\n- cuore/tests/check_dossier_page.py — its one bare `/v/{VIN}` dossier-content check now hits `/v/{VIN}/dossier`.\n\nVerified for real on the Stelvio (ZASFAKPN5J7B88115): next_action = \"Cannot verify yet: the EVAP monitor will not run above 85 % fuel (set at 93.73 %)... Meanwhile: Inspect the recirculation-line quick-connect (S2125000002).\" — real bulletin, real part numbers (e.g. 04861961AD), real tool names from mes.parts/mes.tools_kb (not the fixture).\n\nHeads-up (not fixed, out of scope / would touch restricted files): several other test files hard-code bare `/v/{VIN}` expecting the old dossier content and will now fail on content assertions (not just status code) since that path is the bench: check_workspace.py (flow-bar check), and likely check_notes_page.py, check_perf.py, check_single_column.py, check_experience_page.py. check_media_page.py fails too, but on an unrelated pre-existing bug (t() undefined in _vbar.html when rendered through media_routes' separate Jinja env) — not caused by this change. Whoever owns those test files will want to repoint their bare `/v/{VIN}` dossier assertions to `/v/{VIN}/dossier`.\n\nOne environment note for future CDP screenshot checks in this repo: a cold freshly-spawned uvicorn process needs to be warmed with one real request before Edge navigates, or Edge's readyState check can read the pre-navigation about:blank document (looks like \"complete\" but body is empty) if the first request (cold mes_bridge.workup + parts/tools resolution) takes longer than the ~1.7s this check waits. check_bench.py now does an explicit warm-up GET before launching Edge; check_screens.py avoids it incidentally via its own seed POST + sleep.\n\nNo commits made, no subagents/forks used, no web search performed, per instructions."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3121,"cache_read_input_tokens":289501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3121,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CDMwUnsKnDfQowNTZkHLf9":{"message":"Bench page built and wired end-to-end; all 4 requested tests pass (check_bench.py 39/39, check_dossier_page.py 42/42, check_dossier_view.py 35/35, check_api.py 96/96 green).\n\nFiles created:\n- cuore/services/bench_bridge.py — build_bench(vin): vehicle name (never unnamed), vin_tail, km, complaint, verdict {state,label,sentence,next_action,blocker}, next_actions (top 3 unchecked steps, ACTIVE families first, each with parts/tools/bulletin/href_tick), open_codes_count, last_read, shortcuts (max 6), case_hint.\n- cuore/web/bench_routes.py — new router, GET /v/{vin} renders bench.html via bench_bridge; reuses the existing POST /v/{vin}/checklist form.\n- cuore/web/templates/bench.html — no hero/step bar, scoped <style> only (cuore.css untouched): 40px status line (name/VIN tail/km/verdict chip) in the vehiclebar block, next_action sentence at 20px, up to 3 big action cards (44px tick button, bulletin chip, parts line, tools w/ have-status), shortcut chips, Job/Full dossier links.\n- cuore/tests/check_bench.py — 5 checks incl. one 400px CDP screenshot (cleanup via _edge_cleanup.kill_edge_profile).\n\nFiles edited:\n- cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py — added verdict.next_action/blocker/next_step_id only, computed in build_view from the existing verdict state, open-work order, and freeze-frame fuel flag (no new judgement, just composes what was already there).\n- cuore/web/routes.py — GET /v/{vin} moved to GET /v/{vin}/dossier (tab stays \"dossier\"); updated module docstring's page table; notes-form redirect updated to the new path.\n- cuore/app.py — registered bench_routes.router (included right after web_routes.router so it claims /v/{vin} now that routes.py no longer does).\n- cuore/web/i18n.py — added full_dossier/mark_done/nothing_open/have_it/need_it (en+it).\n- cuore/tests/check_dossier_page.py — its one bare `/v/{VIN}` dossier-content check now hits `/v/{VIN}/dossier`.\n\nVerified for real on the Stelvio (ZASFAKPN5J7B88115): next_action = \"Cannot verify yet: the EVAP monitor will not run above 85 % fuel (set at 93.73 %)... Meanwhile: Inspect the recirculation-line quick-connect (S2125000002).\" — real bulletin, real part numbers (e.g. 04861961AD), real tool names from mes.parts/mes.tools_kb (not the fixture).\n\nHeads-up (not fixed, out of scope / would touch restricted files): several other test files hard-code bare `/v/{VIN}` expecting the old dossier content and will now fail on content assertions (not just status code) since that path is the bench: check_workspace.py (flow-bar check), and likely check_notes_page.py, check_perf.py, check_single_column.py, check_experience_page.py. check_media_page.py fails too, but on an unrelated pre-existing bug (t() undefined in _vbar.html when rendered through media_routes' separate Jinja env) — not caused by this change. Whoever owns those test files will want to repoint their bare `/v/{VIN}` dossier assertions to `/v/{VIN}/dossier`.\n\nOne environment note for future CDP screenshot checks in this repo: a cold freshly-spawned uvicorn process needs to be warmed with one real request before Edge navigates, or Edge's readyState check can read the pre-navigation about:blank document (looks like \"complete\" but body is empty) if the first request (cold mes_bridge.workup + parts/tools resolution) takes longer than the ~1.7s this check waits. check_bench.py now does an explicit warm-up GET before launching Edge; check_screens.py avoids it incidentally via its own seed POST + sleep.\n\nNo commits made, no subagents/forks used, no web search performed, per instructions."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"